<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY'S MKB TO CUT PRIME RATE TO 22.40 PCT.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY'S MKB TO CUT PRIME RATE TO 22.40 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Magyar Kulkereskedelmi Bank Rt (MKB) will cut its prime lending rate on forint loans to 22.40 percent from 22.75 percent, effective March 3, the bank said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>MKB is majority-owned by Germany's Bayerische Landesbank Girozentrale .</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
